# A point-to-point mountain road. Distances are metres; angles are degrees.
name "Alpine Run"
description "Climb the pass, cross the viaduct, and carry speed over the summit jump."
width 12
start 0 0 0

# A friendly opening straight and a sweeping right into the hills.
straight 180
right 55 radius 120 rise 12 bank -12
straight 110 rise 9 bank 0
checkpoint

# A left sweep opens onto an elevated bridge.
left 70 radius 105 rise 5 bank 14
bridge 160 rise 3 bank 0
straight 80 rise -4
checkpoint

# The road curves through a covered mountain gallery.
right 70 radius 100 rise 6 bank -10 kind tunnel
tunnel 130 rise 4 bank 0
left 45 radius 110 rise 4 bank 12
straight 100 bank 0
checkpoint

# Gentle launch: the 14 m gap has no road or collision surface.
# Arrive straight with speed. The landing is 2.5 m below the lip.
straight 90
ramp 24 rise 2.5
gap 14 rise -2.5
straight 100
checkpoint

# A downhill pair of bends leads into a broad finish straight.
right 80 radius 95 rise -12 bank -14
straight 100 rise -8 bank 0
left 55 radius 110 rise -10 bank 12
straight 200 rise -9 bank 0
finish
